# WP1 examples 0121: pre-edit evidence and requirement inventory

Observed HEAD 94374c7a708f32b9d466614aa4c566184ac9165b, tree 74af6b6a919c2df6845e38da89604e80479584d6, clean before authoring. All nine Context pins matched actual bytes, including the staged reviewer input. Review #581 observed 19d43f01e6022a8ab269f04b2b88c12c98bf53b3, tree f08b518974955b5ab746f027123cd97322f23aa3; this checkout differs through later commits. Scoped-byte identity, rather than HEAD equality, is the prerequisite. No material mismatch found.

The fenced record below was saved before package/checker/reviewer-copy authoring. Protected pins cover every pre-existing writing file, the complete real-project-0107 directory, sources metadata (hashes only; content not inspected), preparation index and source contracts. No historical checker/audit or reviewer check was executed. Startup diagnostics declare claude-sonnet-5-5; the continued parent candidate declares codex/gpt-6.1-sol, so exact model continuity is not certified. This author is exposed, not a cold independent reviewer.

## Derived requirements and availability

The machine-readable leaf inventory below gives exact source locators, literal values and hashes; counts and IDs are re-derived from those bytes, not copied from issue summaries.

- Task /tasks/4 has 1 semantic, 4 preservation and 3 answer IDs: {"semantic_ids": ["WP1-property-text"], "preservation_ids": ["WP1-other-project-bytes", "WP1-file-set-and-unrelated-files", "WP1-root-version-declaration", "WP1-original-and-license"], "answer_ids": ["WP1-describe-text-delta", "WP1-original-output-grounding", "WP1-honest-limits"]}. The preservation map must cover all four preservation IDs plus the text relation.
- /common/answer_rule and protocol L26/L29 require original and corresponding output artifact hashes, paths and exact supporting locations, conditions, limitations, all atomic required claims, extras and contradictions; L35/L36 and /required_ids/6/separate_dimension_tests keep relational correctness and evidence grounding separate. L40 fixes denominators; L41 separately assesses required claims and extras; L60 requires independent review and blocks disputed key use. Narrative truth still needs human adjudication.
- /tasks/4/request, /text_contract and README L54 require the unique pinned property, exact preconditions, 2 to 3 at byte 3347/line 42, complete project bytes and no other changed byte. /preservation and README L56 require BOM, XML declaration, tabs, LF, entities, order, final newline, other properties including autoIncrement, unchanged file set, immutable original and license outside writable roots, before/after hashes and delivered MIT notice.
- /common/preflight/0 and /3, /common/artifact_record/2 through /8, /tasks/4/output_manifest_rule, /trial_artifacts/manifest_rule and /required_ids/2/original_output_citation_rule require frozen pre/post workspace AND dependency inventories: every present path, kind, size, SHA256 and complete raw-byte reference, missing/unexpected paths, boundaries, unchanged unrelated files and no links/resolution into originals or other arms. /required_ids/4 requires complete immutable original/license before/after and delivered notice evidence.
- /finding_dispositions/F4/missing_evidence/0 through /2 and /claim_adjudication/prescribed_ledgers/0/evidence_reservation plus /2/evidence_reservation retain those same missing inventory, immutable/license and every-preservation-ID map requirements; both raw answers remain incomplete and both historical map slots blocked. No unseen sidecar may be assumed.
- /tasks/4/trial_artifacts/required has 13 entries, each individually listed below. Complete source/expected-project/notice bytes and authored inventory/map controls can be supplied. Actual failed outputs, errors/truncation/retries, request-response/tool logs, time/cost/budgets, native logs and per-file native save-version evidence are unavailable: no trial, agent arm or LabVIEW execution exists. Mark these unavailable, not empty successful results.
- /tasks/4/originals/0/save_version, /oracle/missing, /native_outcome, /planned_results, /reading_fidelity, /common/native_rule, README L60/L62/L64 and protocol L34/L38/L39 require explicit native, reader, dependency, allocation/isolation and independent-approval gaps. Dependency URL declarations can be exhaustively enumerated from the pinned XML, but referenced dependency bytes, transitive closure and actual resolution are unavailable. Missing entries must have null size/hash/raw-byte reference with a reason; do not invent dependencies, sidecars or a complete native closure.
- A complete positive example is an authored conditional map over the explicitly enumerated workspace/immutable/notice bytes and declared-but-absent references, not proof of a real complete trial or dependency closure. Logical root separation and no-resolution conditions are stipulated controls, never tested runner isolation. The unmeasured startup-time extra remains unverified/missing. Neither example can release F4.

