    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L26",
      "value": "Gradeable answer record: `case_id`, `status`, `claims[{claim_id, answer, conditions, citations[]}]`, `limitations`. Citations contain original SHA256, repository-relative path, archive/member chain when applicable, and a native object/property locator or exact XML/key/byte location appropriate to the claim.",
      "value_sha256": "cca0825eefc847f07762abc661a00ab806d95d30fa1cd9e373ffba9f1d32d55b"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L27",
      "value": "For diagrams, record owning VI, nested structure/case, object/terminal/wire identity and native view region; attach a hashed native capture and object map when identifiers are unstable. A screenshot or exported node ID alone is insufficient: the reviewer must resolve the claim back into the preserved original.",
      "value_sha256": "3d2aea18772cf319847cc1c86688b634fe5bc2c6d6c0ddcd145520774b296ad3"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L28",
      "value": "Before reader exposure, freeze an independently checked reference inventory per task: stable required-claim IDs, atomic facts/relations, conditions, acceptable alternatives, numerical tolerances, original/native reference locators and hashes, and disallowed inferences. Identify separately the required answer claims and required reader observations; neither inventory may be inferred from submitted answers or exports. Record inventory/key revisions and unresolved references. Development keys may be public; withheld keys, case details and revealing evidence must never enter this repository or its history.",
      "value_sha256": "022e27d53eb08261ddd5ab38239c713edefaf5f284dcbd44d9257dbd48009ea8"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L29",
      "value": "Account for every required ID and every submitted factual assertion, including implicit assertions in prose and limitations. Preserve the submitted text and its mapping to reference IDs; split compound assertions into atomic claims under frozen rules. Repeated equivalent assertions earn credit once; omissions retain their required slots. An assertion and its negation are a contradiction even when one matches the key: mark the affected item incorrect and retain both assertions. Unmatched assertions enter a separate extra-claim ledger and require independent checking; true extras cannot replace omissions, and false or unverified extras cannot disappear from scoring. Freeze these mapping/adjudication rules before runs and retain scorer/checker decisions.",
      "value_sha256": "2d677d5e97afd2d32c8da58e353475d1c5bb0c42cbf65f12e69a6bd1b3e50dc0"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L30",
      "value": "Score reading fidelity, answer correctness and source grounding separately using the following item rules; faithful extraction alone does not establish correct reasoning, and answer correctness cannot establish fidelity.",
      "value_sha256": "736eabfaa3a8aad86930063bb13f2653803cfad1afaac198557ff83d62fdf877"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
