    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L38",
      "value": "Reader-observation contract: before exposure, an independent preparer freezes probe IDs, artifact/member hashes, reader entry points and arguments, observation scope, required observation IDs and native-reference alignment rules. Choose probes from the task/native inventories, independently of agent answers and reader outputs; include the types, objects, wires, properties and relationships needed by the task. Pin ordering, limits, any adaptive branches and their selection rules; record unprobed scope as missing coverage. No favorable agent-selected calls may substitute for required probes.",
      "value_sha256": "a940442c18839635890f4fb1282e2b4aafe65df620d405298356e64fc3bde36d"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L39",
      "value": "For every probe, preserve the exact request, reader/configuration revision, environment, raw response bytes or files and hashes, timestamps, exit/error records and any truncation. Preserve empty responses and failed calls. A separate alignment record maps raw-output locations to required native-reference IDs and records absent, extra, duplicate and contradictory assertions; normalization must retain raw evidence and cannot invent missing facts. Unsupported operations, missing dependencies/licenses/environment, protected/removed diagrams, empty or truncated required content, errors and unverified references never count as matching observations. A successful call or valid wrapper alone earns no fidelity credit.",
      "value_sha256": "4150e219dd01adea5cc9a3a9e7e3e0fcd6ce3dd673795ad882be7c140604af38"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L40",
      "value": "Freeze denominators per task and dimension: all required answer IDs for correctness and grounding, and all required observation IDs for fidelity. Report counts in every item-outcome category over those fixed totals, plus separate extra-claim counts by outcome and contradiction/duplicate counts; do not enlarge denominators with submitted claims or remove unavailable items. Report all planned cases as the coverage denominator alongside attempted/executed/scored counts. Any conditional summary must also show its eligible denominator and excluded/unavailable counts; no single aggregate merges the three dimensions.",
      "value_sha256": "4d49481a47a81d7dd802030c2b3d078b125d4998d809a2ba2f0c624c1c2031a9"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L41",
      "value": "Apply the following case-assessment rules in order, separately for each dimension. An absent or empty required reference inventory is unverified, never vacuously correct. With an established inventory, any incorrect required item or extra assertion, including a false assertion, contradiction or non-supporting citation in grounding, makes that dimension incorrect. Otherwise, any unverified required item or extra makes it unverified. Otherwise, every required item and extra must be correct (fully supported for grounding) for a correct assessment. Of the remaining cases, any correct/partial required item or extra makes the assessment partial; otherwise any tool error makes it error; otherwise all required items unsupported makes it unsupported; all other combinations of missing/unsupported items make it missing. Keep operational limitations and their affected IDs alongside this assessment; partial, missing, unsupported, unverified and error outcomes never become full passes. These are accounting rules, not owner quality thresholds.",
      "value_sha256": "dce65c180ede85bdb0fe812ef4b582f6e97b35be89fce0b1a29f67de9fee80e0"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/protocol.md",
      "locator": "L60",
      "value": "An independent checker must resolve each expected claim and citation against original/native evidence without using the reader's output to derive the answer. Record case/key revision, evidence hashes, checker identity/role and session, procedure, claim-level agreement/disagreement and unresolved uncertainty. Disagreement blocks that claim's use as an established key until adjudicated and rechecked.",
      "value_sha256": "957d44ffe26ffa57ef3c79a80f72850a30aee67322e4bb0a588fb8eb03adccbe"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/writing/README.md",
      "locator": "L54",
      "value": "In a later isolated writable `Core/AF PPL Build.lvproj`, require the complete original SHA256 `1d5e140df788ce1f91c89241bbdb1227c5e4cc6fdf6efbbd820974bbe6082dcf` (5806 bytes), root `Project Type=\"Project\" LVVersion=\"20008000\"`, and exactly one `/Project/Item[@Name='My Computer']/Item[@Name='Build Specifications']/Item[@Name='AF PPL']/Property[@Name='Bld_version.build']` with `Type=\"Int\"`, no children and exact text `2`. Change only `2` to requested `3`: byte 3347 (zero based), line 42, hex `32` to `33`, unchanged size. Stop on any failed precondition. No project file is edited in this integration.",
      "value_sha256": "8698575ee9b012ea25f209b029e1a06e8f118776c576469f2f814b38825db41d"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/writing/README.md",
      "locator": "L56",
      "value": "Preserve all other bytes/files, BOM, XML declaration, tabs, LF, entity spelling, ordering, final newline and `Bld_autoIncrement=true`; no resave or metadata exception. Keep the complete original and MIT notice immutable outside writable arms, hash before/after, and retain complete edited bytes, file/dependency inventories, original/output source map, raw failures and accounting. Root `LVVersion=20008000` is a declaration only; WP1 original `save_version` remains unavailable. Neither that declaration nor the build-version property supplies native save-version authority, build behavior or WB1's source/build chain.",
      "value_sha256": "bc5e377857a7c467ac845bcbf1eee5d2e8fe98c01ce467c6f32667c4ce412c0c"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/writing/README.md",
      "locator": "L58",
      "value": "The distinct `project_text` controls derive in-memory byte fixtures from the pinned original. One positive and 30 fixed rejecting controls check no-op, wrong locator/value/precondition/original/allowance, unrelated bytes/files, missing/extra output, original overwrite, BOM/declaration/line-ending/entity/final-newline rewrites, duplicate locator, wrong property type, root-version drift and unsupported native/dependency/build/behavior/save-version/overall passes. Four of those controls also reject promoting the root declaration to native save version, inventing a native key or overall pass, and dropping WP1 from the method inventory. Exact inventory and reasons are asserted independently of the fixture list. The existing 44 synthetic rejections remain unchanged. No edited project is emitted and these examples are no trial.",
      "value_sha256": "e41b3c8f7bffbf8b7d15a9ddc950b9e902642967def338893a688ff01e5059f3"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/writing/README.md",
      "locator": "L60",
      "value": "WP1 text and root-declaration trial results remain `unexecuted`; native validity, dependencies, build and behavior remain `unexecuted`; native save version and overall writing remain `unverified`. A positive preparation fixture supplies neither an answer scorer nor an overall writing pass. C1 remains open: structured controls and integrity hashes do not establish arbitrary narrative or future answers; independent semantic, extra-claim, contradiction and original/output citation review remains required.",
      "value_sha256": "d8c496277f6a7ef07809cb2d51f899bdda6c7df4a8a5df169064867d4060cb0d"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/writing/README.md",
      "locator": "L62",
      "value": "Before either arm, a separate preparer/checker must approve and freeze every text/preservation/answer ID, prompt, original/workspace/dependency manifests, allowed inputs, documentation and key revision with identities, hashes, agreement and uncertainty. Full native keys/locators/validation remain pending. Inherit the matched comparison and isolation requirements above: actual model/settings/budgets/retries/repetitions/quota/arm order, fresh sessions/workspaces, symmetric editing/output bytes, complete failure slots and post-freeze separate trusted native validation. None is allocated or executed here.",
      "value_sha256": "a3240c9eaeab913d0ebe813902ea35f18e799d2c69a28005caf131cb3c9f7655"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/writing/README.md",
      "locator": "L64",
      "value": "This public Actor Framework derivative is familiar-possible and remains in its one development lineage. Whole-lineage restricted allocation and executed allowed/denied/leakage tests remain pending; store readiness is insufficient. WP1 covers one text substitution only: direct creation, LVLIB, other properties/projects and all untested families/versions remain uncovered. W2's text-preparation qualification waives no native/full-trial prerequisite.",
      "value_sha256": "c101200ad5c1f05db66405cf5486917b86f1859a79f2a2c6f6dfaf64547a670b"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmark/writing/README.md",
      "locator": "L66",
      "value": "The single verifier command above also validates the new provenance and unchanged historical pins. It records its own hash and all read input hashes; `verification.json` stores actual stdout/output hashes separately to avoid circular self-hashes. Historical `input-pins.json`, `review-corrections.json`, proposal/checker/reviews, original/license and preparation index stay unchanged. The frozen #544 checker intentionally ceases to match current writing inputs; do not execute it on this integration or refresh its pins. Its results apply only at its pinned historical tree. Owner acceptance of the independently reviewed method, evaluator changes by separate Policymaker order/verifier and product authorization remain pending; this session issues no owner request or readiness promotion.",
      "value_sha256": "f39da57c87b7022a3760d1f5759b7dc7b01f93f64c4f91174713943ae2bf0c79"
    },
